Quest segment A with a save and load while the inn scene runs (test plan step 4), 2026-11-11 10:55-12:06
Probe DLL APBQuestProbe.dll SHA-256 580C457384A54B23811761F44FF0C8BBE0C17F7188AE5133AA126067B10D0407 (06:45 build)
Commands, one after the other (six launches of two trials):
  build/catchup/run-quest-series.ps1 -Prefix qms-1 -Order off,acc,skip -Trials 2 -MidSave 1
  build/catchup/run-quest-series.ps1 -Prefix qms-2 -Order skip,acc,off -Trials 2 -MidSave 1
Profile APB-CatchUp-Test, FramerateLimit 30, start save APB_MQ203_A, game window in front 100% in all 12 trials, dropped rows 0.
"off" = VM catch-up not installed; "acc" = accelerate with the release read rule; "skip" = the same plus the test rule
SetSkipBlocked. Four trials per condition. In each trial the probe takes a snapshot when MQ203 reaches stage 50 (the scene is at
phase 14 or 15), saves, loads that save, takes a second snapshot about 13 s after the first, and lets the scene run to its end.

RESULT
- 12 of 12 trials ended normally. No hang, no failed load, no dump. guard_violations 0 in the eight catch-up trials.
- After the load the scene went on from the phase it was saved in (14 or 15) through phase 29 in every trial; MQ203 reached
  stage 60; the end state (digest 995561791e), the dialogue order (fdb15642cc) and the end state after a second save and load
  are the same in all 12 trials and the same as in the main run without a mid save.
- The snapshot after the load is identical in all 12 trials of the three conditions (one distinct snapshot).
- The snapshot before the save differs between trials in one line, the MQ203 objectives, and not by condition alone:
  [10:3,20:1] (the stage-50 fragment had finished) in off x2, acc x2, skip x4; [10:3,20:0] in off x1, acc x2; [10:1,20:0] in
  off x1. The snapshot is taken the moment stage 50 is seen, so it catches the fragment's two objective calls at whatever
  point they have reached. In the four trials caught partway, the objectives after the load are [10:3,20:1] like everywhere
  else: the fragment's remaining calls ran. Whether the save itself still held them as waiting calls or they finished in
  the moment between the snapshot and the save is not recorded.
- The analysis script prints "mid reload equal: False" for every trial, off included. That compares the two snapshots, which
  are 13 s apart in a running scene (phase 14/15 -> 16, the actors' packages change with it). It is not a difference between
  the saved and the loaded state.
- Graph event -> stage 48 notification 65-68 ms. No menu other than HUD and loading, player not moved, in all 12 trials.
- Every launch left two crash logs right after the window was closed, as before; no address of this project in the stack
  section of any of the 12.

WHAT THIS SHOWS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
- Shows: with catch-up running (either rule), a save made while the scene and its quest stage fragment are in progress loads
  and the scene completes with the same end state as without catch-up, in four trials each.
- Does not show: a save made at other moments (only stage 50 was used), other quests, 42 FPS, the release DLL.

